{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git show bd462723:collab/yang-clojure/1795112272000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r4.glm-5.3.findings.md; git show bd462723:collab/yang-clojure/1795109958000-reviewer-fixorder-r3.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md; git show bd462723:collab/yang-clojure/1795109079000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r3.glm-5.3.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-19 18:30:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-20 01:30:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: glm\nSession-ID: 3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\nRole: Compiler Engineer (compiler provenance)\nImplementers:\n- Model: glm-5.3 | Status: r3 review P2 + two P3s resolved | Rationale: r4 narrow fix round over reviewer 1795109958000\n\n# fix/constructed-collection-order r4 — the three review findings resolved\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder @ 7e6d720c plus the r3\nrepairs (uncommitted) plus this round, NOTHING COMMITTED. Three changes\nonly, per the dispatch: the set-trace test, the fixture docstring digest,\nand the Jupiter mirror README.\n\n## P2 (blocker) — distinct labels + a discriminating mutation counter-check\n\nset-effect-order-and-collision-trace-test now gives each colliding\nelement its own tap label while keeping the collision:\n(do (tap :left) (- n 1)) and (do (tap :right) (- 1 n)) at n=1 -- both\nreturn 0, so the set value still collides. The expected label sequence is\nderived from the existing independent element-root sort and asserted on\nall four routes ([:s1 :left :right]), with the final\n#{:s1 0 2} kept-once assertion retained.\n\nDiscrimination evidence (the dispatch offered red-then-green or an\nin-test counter-check; this round ships the counter-check, and the red\nside is the reviewer's own documented probe):\n- IN-TEST (permanent): the test extracts the two compiled colliding\n  operands, mutates the COMPILED tree with postwalk-replace -- (a) the\n  pair exchanged, (b) one duplicated over the other -- and asserts on\n  every route that the observed trace CHANGES: the swap yields exactly\n  the label exchange, the duplicate evaluates :left twice and :right\n  never. Under the r3 form (both operands tapping 0) these same\n  mutations were invisible -- the reviewer's probe measured identical\n  [:s1 0 0] traces and identical results for original/swap/duplicate on\n  all four routes -- so these assertions could not have passed before;\n  they now pin the assertions' discriminating power, not just the\n  emitter's behavior.\n- Reviewer probe (red side, quoted from 1795109958000 findings): with\n  distinct labels the original/swap/duplicate traces were\n  [:s1 :left :right] / [:s1 :right :left] / [:s1 :left :left] on the JVM\n  -- exactly what the in-test counter-check now asserts.\n\n## P3 — fixture docstring digest\n\nThe docstring now carries the full 64-digit sha256\n9673c6143af2f20e74d7321f493784a145251c7cf8b758294cba1abfa15f49b2\n(the r3 text had dropped a digit in its hyphenated grouping);\nverified to match the fixture file bytes.\n\n## P3 — Jupiter mirror README\n\nThe README no longer claims Node+Dart green from bbtest.out. The\ncorrected text states exactly what each file covers, verified against\nthe files: bbtest.out is the JVM attempt of bb test only (5,181 tests /\n400,386 assertions / 11 failures, ending at \"Error while executing task:\ntest:clj\"; the log contains no test:cljs/test:cljd output -- the run\nstopped at the failing JVM task) and establishes no Node or Dart\nfull-quick result; daostream.out (JVM 589 / Node 579 / Dart 509, all\nexit 0) is the mirror's only tri-host result. The correction is noted\nin place as the r4 change.\n\n## Gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| JVM ordering namespace | 15 tests, 91,500 assertions, 0 failures (r3: 91,477; +23 = the relabeled set trace + the mutation counter-check) |\n| kondo on the touched test file | 0 errors, 0 warnings (exit 0; the pre-existing yin.repl.query warning lives in the callsite file, not in this round's scope) |\n\nNode and Dart were NOT rerun this round: the dispatch scoped the rerun to\nthe JVM ordering namespace, and the changed surface (tap labels in one\ntest, a docstring, a README) is host-neutral; the four-route trace\nassertions themselves run on every lane whenever those lanes execute.\nB1 (Jolt) remains the J2 owner's external dependency, unchanged.\n\n## Files\n\n- test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc: the set-trace rewrite\n  (distinct labels, operand-carrying-label helper, mutation\n  counter-check) + the docstring digest.\n- collab/yang-clojure/1795110000000-jupiter-g2-gate-evidence/README.md:\n  the coverage correction (an evidence file, not code).\n- New evidence: collab/yang-clojure/1795112272000-fixorder-r4-evidence/\n  (kondo log). Temporary driver namespace deleted at delivery.\n\nSHA-256 pins at delivery:\n| File | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc | 869492520185fd2ec486a7febf1cd133f753f34920e4be85319ae10b3a53b0ec |\n| collab/yang-clojure/1795110000000-jupiter-g2-gate-evidence/README.md | 93446079b1ef25a8174d96153cbf941fcf90b374e530a6c4930a3c470fae99c5 |\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-19 17:48:12 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-20 00:48:12 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nRole: Reviewer (compiler provenance)\nCoding-Agent: codex\n\n# fixorder r3 review\n\n**REMAINING-FINDINGS**\n\nB2 and the JVM/Node/Dart portion of B3 are satisfied. B4 remains open for the set collision trace. B1 remains open with the J2 owner. The Jupiter mirror also needs a correction to its full-suite lane claim.\n\n## Actionable findings\n\n### P2 — B4 set trace cannot distinguish the colliding occurrences\n\nBoth colliding operands emit the same `0` event because the test's `tap` logs and returns its argument. The expected trace therefore identifies two zero events in aggregate. In a JVM probe, I used the actual compiled set AST and ran the original, a variant with the two colliding operands swapped, and a variant with one of them duplicated in place of the other. All three produced `[:s1 0 0]` and `#{:s1 0 2}` on the walker, semantic, stack, and register routes. The assertions accept both altered executions. The architect specifically required canonical effect order and exactly-once evaluation of each colliding occurrence. [Set trace](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L1045)\n\nGive each colliding expression its own tap label while keeping both return values equal to `0`. For example, use `(do (tap :left) (- n 1))` and `(do (tap :right) (- 1 n))`. Derive the expected label sequence from the existing independent element-root sort, assert it on all four routes, and retain the final set assertion. I checked this alternative in memory on the JVM. Every route produced `[:s1 :left :right]` for the original, `[:s1 :right :left]` for the swap, and `[:s1 :left :left]` for the duplicate. The result set stayed `#{:s1 0 2}` in each case.\n\n### P3 — The fixture docstring drops a digit from the SHA-256\n\nAfter removing separators, the docstring yields 63 hex digits. It has `…493784a14525c7cf…` where the independently verified digest has `…493784a145251c7cf…`. The binary and the engineer findings carry the correct digest. Copy the full 64-digit SHA-256 into the docstring. [Fixture docstring](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L1221)\n\n### P3 — Jupiter mirror overstates full-suite lane coverage\n\nThe mirror README labels `bbtest.out` as a full quick tri-host run with Node and Dart green. The saved command ends at `Error while executing task: test:clj`, after 5,181 tests, 400,386 assertions, and 11 failures. `bb test` lists the JVM test task before the Node and Dart test tasks, and this log contains no results for those later tasks. The separate `dao.stream` log shows all three lanes passing. Correct the README to scope the full quick result to the JVM attempt, or attach any separately saved full Node and Dart results with their tested revision. [Mirror README](1795110000000-jupiter-g2-gate-evidence/README.md#L8) · [Full quick log](1795110000000-jupiter-g2-gate-evidence/bbtest.out#L1366) · [Task definition](../../bb.edn#L343)\n\n## Dispositions and evidence\n\n- **Scope verified.** `HEAD` is `7e6d720c` and the tracked r3 diff contains only the ordering test (+436/−27) and the restored fixture (11 to 5,403 bytes). The emitter, frontend manifest, callsite suite, cc4 fixtures, J2 inventory and tracked r1/r2 findings match `HEAD`. The active cc4 snapshot still hashes to `093f903a62e780a665ee2da107a1630126385f53b028d14e236031d48a70e5c1`. `git diff --check` passes. The historical raw red log also matches its recorded digest.\n- **B2 satisfied.** I decoded the base64 text independently from `HEAD` and the worktree. Both decode to the exact file bytes, SHA-256 `9673c6143af2f20e74d7321f493784a145251c7cf8b758294cba1abfa15f49b2`. On the JVM the decoded payload identifies `c1-1`, root `:segment/blake3-49d9ef3191b305b26e67a803c9e74104dc57d1c5f036147b3fd2352d256f5e64`, and old value `{0 :b}`. The custody test uses NIO, Node `fs`, and Dart I/O behind a `:cljd`-gated require. It compares the bytes, validates the decoded root row, and loads the file's rows to assert the old result without recompiling. [Custody test](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L1322)\n- **B3 satisfied on the three evidenced hosts.** I recomputed all 16 pinned shuffle vectors using both unnormalized exact integer arithmetic and normalized Node `Number` arithmetic. The vectors matched at sizes 8, 9, 16, and 32 across all recorded seeds. I also ran the extracted JVM generator for seed `1795017757000` at all four sizes. Its size-8 vector is `[3 0 1 2 5 7 6 4]`, matching the Node recomputation and the architect's JVM column. The first reduction limits every product to at most `103661183027795`, below `2^53`. The 18-case literal bundle pins each root, application count, digest of the full canonical-sorted C1 relation and occurrence-key vector, and digest of the semantic, stack, and register provenance tuple. Every host checks that same bundle and the existing permutation and representation properties still run. [Generator](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L262) · [Reference check](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L1520)\n- **Float dependency handling accepted.** The saved first Node run fails precisely at the `0.0`-bearing case with different root and relation/provenance digests. The CBOR profile assigns portable float-kind preservation to the producer. A bare integral JavaScript Number such as positive `0.0` encodes as integer content, while a JVM `Double` encodes as float64. Archiving the failure and keeping non-integral float cases in the shared gate is transparent and within the collection-order bounds. The documented dependency remains open. [Numeric identity contract](../../docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md#L387) · [Archived Node failure](1795104744000-fixorder-r3-evidence/fixorder-r3-node-order-floats-divergence.log)\n- **Other B4 controls satisfied.** The metadata fixture holds the source form constant apart from `{:sem true}` and checks that `{}` gives the plain root. The failure fixtures derive the expected taps using standalone child roots and the canonical comparator. I independently checked that the fixtures exercise `[]` and `[:pre :v]`. Both cases require exact `{:order-test :boom}` on every route. The raw AST fixture captures at lambda entry and invokes the captured continuation from an operand of an assoc-over-seed application. Every route must return `:done` and log exactly `[:early :early-v]`, excluding `:never`. [Metadata](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L673) · [Failure](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L892) · [Transfer](../../test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc#L1003)\n- **B1 remains open.** Both historical Jolt logs show the same four `UNLISTED` namespaces and stop at inventory validation. The r3 delivery records zero Jolt children and contains no simulated comparison. J2 owns inventory reconciliation and the targeted Jolt reruns. [Jolt ordering refusal](1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jolt-order.log) · [Jolt callsite refusal](1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jolt-callsite.log)\n\n## Gate counts\n\n| Evidence | Verified result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Independent JVM rerun of both namespaces | 61 tests / 92,082 assertions, zero failures or errors, exit 0 |\n| Archived JVM ordering and callsite | 15 tests / 91,477 assertions and 46 / 605. Both green, for 61 tests / 92,082 assertions in total |\n| Archived Node ordering | Final 15 / 91,477, zero failures or errors. Earlier 15 / 91,477, one float divergence |\n| Archived Dart ordering | All 15 named tests passed. The runner reports test count |\n| Archived clj-kondo | Zero errors and one existing callsite unused-require warning |\n| Jupiter `dao.stream` | JVM 589, Node 579, Dart 509 tests. All three exit 0 |\n| Jupiter focused comparison | Detached master 18 / 6,192 and merged branch 18 / 6,193. Both contain the same two failure signatures. The store-write audit expectation and actual maps are equal across the two logs when compared as parsed data |\n\nThe archived JVM, Node, Dart and lint logs are under [r3 evidence](1795104744000-fixorder-r3-evidence/). The Jupiter evidence covers pre-r3 revisions. The focused master and branch comparison reproduces both lint failures on master, and the nine arm-violation failures from the earlier JVM quick run are absent in the merged branch comparison. [Jupiter mirror](1795110000000-jupiter-g2-gate-evidence/)\n\nThe JVM rerun used the cached test classpath with `java -cp \"$(cat .cpcache/3644903311.cp)\" clojure.main -m cognitect.test-runner -n yang.clojure-collection-order-test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test`. Node and Dart counts come from the archived ordering runs. This review authored only this findings file.\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-19 16:45:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-19 23:45:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: glm\nSession-ID: 3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\nRole: Compiler Engineer (compiler provenance)\nImplementers:\n- Model: glm-5.3 | Status: blockers B2/B3/B4 repaired, gates green on JVM/Node/Dart; B1 external, recorded open | Rationale: r3 fix round over architect sign-off 1795101450000\n\n# fix/constructed-collection-order r3 — B2, B3, B4 repaired (B1 external)\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder @ 7e6d720c plus this\nround's edits, NOTHING COMMITTED. The emitter, manifest, cohort re-pin and\nJ2 inventory are untouched (verified clean by the sign-off). Per the r3\nbounds, this round changes only test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc,\nthe legacy fixture under test/resources/yang/clojure/, and new evidence\nfiles. The r1/r2 findings are not rewritten.\n\n## B2 — the retained binary artifact restored\n\nThe r1 capture had spit a Java byte-array toString into the fixture path\n(11 bytes, \"[B@257c7d2d\"); the sign-off independently verified the\nEMBEDDED base64 payload as the real artifact (5,403 bytes, sha256\n9673c6143af2f20e74d7321f493784a145251c7cf8b758294cba1abfa15f49b2). The\nfixture file now holds exactly those decoded bytes -- corrected digest\n9673c614...15f49b2 (the old bogus d4fa698d... pin described those 11\nbytes and is superseded here, not rewritten into history). New\nlegacy-fixture-custody-test (portable byte reading in the\nyin.repl.store-test raw content-log pattern: nio / fs / dart-io, the\nlatter behind a :cljd-gated require) asserts on every host:\n- both custody copies are 5,403 bytes and byte-EQUAL (bytes/equal? of the\n  file against the decoded embedded copy);\n- the file's payload decodes, carries the c1-1 revision and the recorded\n  root, executes through ast-walker/vm-load-rows to the recorded old\n  value {0 :b} without recompilation.\nThe embedded-copy legacy family continues to run as before; the docstring\nnow states the corrected digest and the custody assertion.\n\n## B3 — the corpus is now a common cross-host replay gate\n\n1. Generator repaired: lcg reduces the seed modulo the modulus BEFORE the\n   first product. The r1 form fed the raw timestamp seed in (first\n   product 86647302148147000 > 2^53), so the JVM's exact long arithmetic\n   and the double hosts diverged -- exactly the sign-off's table (JVM\n   639147076 vs Node 639147084). After reduction every product is below\n   2^53; the JVM column is unchanged (exact arithmetic makes the\n   reduction a no-op there), and the double hosts join it.\n2. Generated vectors pinned: corpus-generator-pins-test compares the two\n   seeded shuffles of every size-8/9/16/32 call against recorded literal\n   vectors (JVM-recorded; printed in the findings evidence). Every host\n   now provably permutes the corpus with the SAME index vectors.\n3. Cross-host reference recorded: corpus-reference pins, for all 18\n   broader-corpus cases (6 map + 4 set labeled cases, sizes 8/9/16/32 for\n   maps and sets), the canonical construction's root, application count,\n   full C1/keys digests and all three instruction formats'\n   call-provenance -- the cc4 cohort's digest model. The new\n   corpus-cross-host-reference-test compares every host to that ONE\n   bundle; the within-host permutation/representation checks stay as\n   additional properties.\n\n### The cross-host gate caught a real divergence on its first run\n\nThe corpus reference earned its keep immediately: the first Node run of\ncorpus-cross-host-reference-test FAILED at :floats while every within-host\ncheck was green everywhere. Diagnosis: the corpus's 0.0 entry is a bare\nINTEGRAL-valued double, and the codec's documented numeric identity\n(dao.host.float / dao.jing.cbor.md) encodes a bare integral Number as an\nINTEGER on the JS host while the JVM wraps every double in the float64\ncarrier -- so that literal mints different content per host. Evidence:\nJVM root for the 0.0-bearing case\n149c168e3b766d703fc230365be4ad940bbcf487e0bff36efff9cf6e3bf08958 vs the\nNode actual d4ee0ca368a18d7cf8010e211e50ed96df6f4ecc39befad11dd9aad01c57d5b1\n(full keys/c1/provenance digests in the archived node log). This is\nencoder/float-carrier territory -- outside this round's bounds -- so it is\nREPORTED as a dependency, not fixed: a frontend or codec round must decide\nwhether bare integral-valued float literals should travel via the float64\ncarrier on every host. Within this round's bounds the corpus now uses\nnon-integral floats (1.5/2.25/-0.5/3.75/2.5, which travel as float64 on\nevery host), the :floats reference row is re-recorded for that corpus, and\nthe boundary comment sits at the corpus entry.\n\n## B4 — the mandated behavioral/metadata assertions strengthened\n\n- Discriminating metadata control: the semantic-metadata block now\n  compares OTHERWISE IDENTICAL maps (same quoted [1 2] key, same dynamic\n  value, same :other entry) whose only difference is {:sem true} inside\n  the quoted key: the roots differ; an empty-metadata variant matches the\n  plain root (no content); the with-sem order stays canonical.\n- Failure boundary on every route: the expected trace is DERIVED (the tap\n  arguments of exactly the pairs sorting strictly before the failing pair\n  by the independent comparator), asserted EQUAL on all four routes, and\n  every route must surface the raise with the exact ex-data\n  {:order-test :boom}. Two fixtures: one with whatever order the pair\n  keys fall in (the boom pair sorts first: prefix []), one with a\n  recorded tap pair that sorts strictly before the boom pair (prefix\n  [:pre :v]). All four routes support raising; there is no unsupported\n  route to record for the exception case.\n- Continuation transfer: continuation-transfer-stops-later-operands-test\n  composes, exactly as yin.vm.continuation-invoke-test composes captures,\n  a raw-AST program in the emitter's EMITTED SHAPE -- an assoc-over-seed\n  application whose operand captures the continuation and invokes it. On\n  all four routes: no raise, the value re-enters the capture point\n  (:done), the pre-transfer operands evaluate exactly once\n  ([:early :early-v]), and the operand after the transfer never\n  evaluates. (The Clojure frontend has no capture syntax, hence raw AST\n  in the emitted shape rather than a yang-compiled form.)\n- Set effect-order trace: set-effect-order-and-collision-trace-test gives\n  the dynamic set's elements tap events, including two expressions that\n  collide at runtime ((tap (- n 1)) and (tap (- 1 n)) at n=1). The\n  expected trace is derived from the independent element roots (canonical\n  order, the untapped literal holding its position without logging);\n  every route consumes the elements in that order, each occurrence\n  exactly once (both colliding taps appear), and the result keeps the\n  collided value once.\n\n## Gates (same command forms as r2, rerun after the repairs)\n\nHost darkstar, Darwin 25.6.0 arm64; OpenJDK 21.0.2+13-58 (mise, child\nprocesses), Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602, Node v26.1.0, Flutter 3.47.8. The\nNode/Dart/kondo forms ran through the temporary r3 driver namespace\n(ProcessBuilder + JAVA_HOME, logs under target/fixorder-r3-*.log,\narchived in the r3 evidence dir; deleted at delivery).\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| JVM ordering | 15 tests, 91,477 assertions, 0 failures (r2: 10/91,392; +5 tests, +85 assertions) |\n| JVM callsite | 46 tests, 605 assertions, 0 failures (unchanged surface, re-verified) |\n| Node ordering | first run 15/91,477 with 1 failure -- the cross-host reference CAUGHT the :floats integral-float divergence (see above); after the corpus repair and re-recorded row, final run 15 tests, 91,477 assertions, 0 failures. Both logs archived |\n| Dart ordering | ALL 15 PASSED (12:57 wall; the earlier pre-floats-repair Dart run had also passed all 10-then-15 tests, this is the delivered file's run) |\n| kondo (touched files) | 0 errors, 1 warning (the pre-existing yin.repl.query unused require), exit 2 |\n\nOne Dart compile repair during the round: the custody test's dart-io\nreader needs a :cljd-gated require (the store-test pattern imports\n\"dart:io\" explicitly); added, JVM/Node re-verified green on the delivered\nfile afterward, and the archived logs are of the delivered file.\n\n## B1 (external, open) and landing evidence\n\n- B1 stands exactly as the sign-off states: the J2 manifest refuses the\n  four inherited unlisted namespaces before any child, so the required\n  Jolt comparison has never executed. It is the J2 owner's dependency;\n  this round neither runs nor simulates it, adds no exclusions, and\n  records zero Jolt children as NOT a pass.\n- Landing evidence: the jupiter g2 gate logs the architect could not\n  certify are now mirrored locally by the orchestrator at\n  collab/yang-clojure/1795110000000-jupiter-g2-gate-evidence/\n  (summary.txt: bbtest-rc=1, daostream-rc=0; bbtest.out: 5,181 tests /\n  400,386 assertions / 11 failures; daostream.out: lane table; plus\n  master-redcheck.out and branch-mergecheck.out carrying the two\n  pre-existing master lint reds the sign-off does not charge to this\n  fix). This round did not fetch them; the requirement is noted and the\n  mirror is cited.\n\n## Files\n\n- test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc: B2 custody test + dart-io\n  require; B3 lcg seed reduction, generator pins, recorded corpus\n  reference + cross-host test; B4 metadata control, failure prefixes,\n  transfer fixture, set trace; the F2/F3 blocks from r2 unchanged.\n- test/resources/yang/clojure/constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor:\n  the true 5,403-byte artifact (corrected sha256 9673c614...15f49b2).\n- New evidence: collab/yang-clojure/1795104744000-fixorder-r3-evidence/\n  (lane logs) and the generator-pin table quoted above.\n- Nothing else; emitter/manifest/cohort/J2 untouched.\n\nSHA-256 pins at delivery (only the first two files changed this round):\n\n| `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc` | `86dffc9ad72f209c70a894b06f36ab755ad58cecc0c2d30b3e62d5093ca46e5c` |\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor` | `9673c6143af2f20e74d7321f493784a145251c7cf8b758294cba1abfa15f49b2` |\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | `4a47a86e0a34107e7e28eef875084be14356814aca1d5d1b1b1e80556dbb7a56` |\n| `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` | `8a3f8132adc061826ff8faa35b134c3366ff3b2d3063cc621fb1d25d52aa3547` |\n| `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | `e489b371e534bb4fabd835552f918d1c744e632e8bfe1103f8388535a74de875` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
