{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show bd462723:test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc | sed -n '276,310p'; git show bd462723:docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md | sed -n '380,405p'; git show bd462723:src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | sed -n '201,221p'; git show bd462723:collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jolt-order.log; git show bd462723:collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jolt-callsite.log; git log --oneline bd462723..master -- src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\"","aggregated_output":"        (recur (conj out x') x' (inc i))))))\n\n\n(defn- lcg-shuffle\n  \"Fisher-Yates over (range n) driven by the recorded-seed Lehmer\n   generator.\"\n  [seed n]\n  (if (< n 2)\n    (vec (range n))\n    (let [states (lcg seed (dec n))]\n      (loop [i (dec n), s states, acc (vec (range n))]\n        (if (zero? i)\n          acc\n          (let [j (mod (first s) (inc i))]\n            (recur (dec i) (rest s)\n                   (assoc acc i (nth acc j) j (nth acc i)))))))))\n\n\n(defn- recorded-permutations\n  \"The recorded permutation set for sizes beyond full enumeration: forward,\n   reverse, four rotations and two seeded shuffles.\"\n  [n seed]\n  [(vec (range n))\n   (vec (reverse (range n)))\n   (rotate 1 (vec (range n)))\n   (rotate 2 (vec (range n)))\n   (rotate 3 (vec (range n)))\n   (lcg-shuffle seed n)\n   (lcg-shuffle (inc seed) n)])\n\n\n(defn- permute\n  \"The entries of `v` reordered by the index vector `p`.\"\n  [v p]\n  (into [] (map v) p))\nshortest head); (3) if the two encodings are the same length too, return\nwhichever sorts first by canonical CBOR bytes, the same unsigned bytewise\norder this profile already uses for map keys and set elements, so no new\nordering machinery is needed for the final, rarely-reached tiebreak. All\nthree cases are independent of argument order and of which host runs them:\n`(min 1 1.0)` and `(min 1.0 1)` both return `1`.\n\n- Provide a portable `float64` constructor/carrier. JavaScript callers use\n  it for integral floating-point values such as `1.0`; ordinary integral\n  JavaScript numbers remain integers, except native negative zero, which\n  is floating-point content so its sign survives. Decoding floating-point content on\n  JavaScript returns the carrier so re-encoding cannot lose its kind.\n  Carrying float kind is the producer's obligation; the codec never infers\n  it. The Python frontend's ruling on meeting it is `yang.antlr.md`\n  section 8.5.5.\n- The JavaScript float64 carrier refuses numeric and default coercion: its\n  `valueOf` throws the refusal `:carrier-coercion` (raised through the\n  codec's refusal helper, so `refusal` reads it; it is not a corpus\n  class and not a lift outcome). `carrier + 1`, `carrier - 1`,\n  `carrier < 3`, `Number(carrier)` and `\"\" + carrier` therefore throw\n  instead of answering a string or a bare Number that lost the float's\n  kind. String conversion is unchanged, since it asks `toString` first:\n  `str`, `String(carrier)`, `.toString()` and `pr-str` print as before.\n  So are equality, hashing, map and set keys, canonical bytes, NaN\n  normalization and signed zero, which read the payload directly; no\n  fixture changes. Only Float64 is hardened; the Decimal and Rational\n(defn- host-integer?\n  \"True for an exact integer in any host carrier, and on JavaScript also\n   for an integral Number beyond +/-(2^53 - 1), which is integer content\n   whose value is already rounded (callers refuse it); never a JS -0.\"\n  [x]\n  (or (integer/exact-integer? x)\n      #?(:cljs (and (number? x) (js/Number.isInteger x)\n                    (not (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)))\n         :default false)))\n\n\n(defn float64?\n  \"True for floating-point content: Double or Float on the JVM, the\n   Float64 carrier or a non-integral, non-finite or negative-zero number\n   on JavaScript, a double on Dart.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x double)\n     :clj (or (instance? Double x) (instance? Float x))\n     :cljs (or (instance? number/Float64 x)\n               (and (number? x) (not (host-integer? x))))))\n\nJ2 manifest FAILED:\nUNLISTED yin.repl.php-parser-test -- test/yin/repl/php_parser_test.cljc\nUNLISTED yin.vm.code-entry-test -- test/yin/vm/code_entry_test.cljc\nUNLISTED yin.vm.machine-data-test -- test/yin/vm/machine_data_test.clj\nUNLISTED yin.vm.provenance-test -- test/yin/vm/provenance_test.cljc\nJ2 manifest FAILED:\nUNLISTED yin.repl.php-parser-test -- test/yin/repl/php_parser_test.cljc\nUNLISTED yin.vm.code-entry-test -- test/yin/vm/code_entry_test.cljc\nUNLISTED yin.vm.machine-data-test -- test/yin/vm/machine_data_test.clj\nUNLISTED yin.vm.provenance-test -- test/yin/vm/provenance_test.cljc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show bd462723:test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc | sed -n '390,575p;600,710p'; git show bd462723:src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '298,380p'; git show bd462723:src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc | sed -n '40,62p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show bd462723:test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc | sed -n '390,575p;600,710p'; git show bd462723:src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '298,380p'; git show bd462723:src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc | sed -n '40,62p'\"","aggregated_output":"  \"n recorded dynamic elements.\"\n  [n]\n  (into [] (map (fn [i] (list '+ 'n i))) (range n)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; RULING 3 test 2: map representation/permutation property\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private quoted-pair-key\n  \"A quoted collection key, one plain and one carrying semantic (non\n   position) metadata inside the literal payload.\"\n  (list 'quote [1 2]))\n\n\n(def ^:private quoted-meta-key\n  ;; a different value than quoted-pair-key: host = ignores metadata, so\n  ;; two metadata-variants of one value cannot coexist as map keys (the\n  ;; host map collapses them); metadata-as-content is asserted separately\n  ;; in the oracle test\n  (list 'quote (with-meta [3 4] {:sem true})))\n\n\n(def ^:private map-corpus\n  \"The recorded corpus of distinct source-entry pairs. Every case holds at\n   least one dynamic expression, so each reaches the emitter as a\n   constructed collection.\"\n  [[:constant-keys-dynamic-values\n    [[:a (list '+ 'n 0)] [:b (list '+ 'n 1)]]]\n   [:dynamic-keys\n    [[(list 'first 'xs) :v1] [(list 'first (list 'rest 'xs)) :v2]]]\n   [:heterogeneous-keys\n    [[:kw (list '+ 'n 0)] [\"str\" 1] [3 1.5] ['sym 2]\n     [quoted-pair-key 3] [quoted-meta-key 4] [true 5] [nil 6]]]\n   [:nested-collections\n    [[:inner-map {:inner (list '+ 'n 1)}]\n     [:inner-set #{(list '+ 'n 2) 3}]\n     [:inner-vec [(list '+ 'n 3)]]\n     [:deep {:a #{[(list '+ 'n 4)]}}]]]\n   ;; non-integral floats only: a bare INTEGRAL-valued double (0.0) is a\n   ;; documented host numeric-identity boundary -- the JVM's codec wraps\n   ;; every double in the float64 carrier while the JS host encodes a bare\n   ;; integral Number as an integer, so such a literal mints different\n   ;; content per host (first caught by the cross-host reference on its\n   ;; first Node run; divergent digests recorded in the r3 findings). That\n   ;; boundary is encoder/float-carrier territory and stays outside this\n   ;; round's bounds; float coverage here uses non-integral doubles, which\n   ;; travel as float64 on every host.\n   [:floats\n    [[1.5 (list '+ 'n 1.5)] [2.25 -0.5] [3.75 2.5]]]\n   [:duplicate-subtrees\n    [[:a (list 'first 'xs)] [:b (list 'first 'xs)] [:c (list 'first 'xs)]]]])\n\n\n(def ^:private map-corpus-sizes\n  \"Sizes crossing the array-map/hash-map representation thresholds; each\n   gets the full recorded permutation set under both representations.\"\n  [8 9 16 32])\n\n\n(deftest map-permutation-invariance-test\n  (testing \"sizes 0-4: every insertion permutation, both representations\"\n    (doseq [n (range 5)\n            :let [entries (sized-map-entries n)]]\n      (testing (str \"size \" n)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:array-map :hash-map]]\n                                         (build-map rep (permute entries p)))))\n                             (all-permutations n))\n              snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (pos? (count variants)))\n          (is (apply = snaps)\n              (str n \"-entry permutations diverge: \"\n                   (pr-str (distinct snaps))))\n          (when (pos? n)\n            (doseq [form variants\n                    :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n              (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n              (is (every? #(strictly-ascending? (pair-keys %)) ctors))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus: permutations of the recorded entries\"\n    (doseq [[label entries] map-corpus]\n      (testing (str label)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:array-map :hash-map]]\n                                         (build-map rep (permute entries p)))))\n                             (all-permutations (count entries)))\n              snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (every? #(strictly-ascending? (pair-keys %)) ctors)))))))\n  (testing \"sizes 8/9/16/32: recorded permutations cross the thresholds\"\n    (doseq [n map-corpus-sizes\n            :let [entries (sized-map-entries n)]]\n      (testing (str \"size \" n)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:array-map :hash-map]]\n                                         (build-map rep (permute entries p)))))\n                             (recorded-permutations n 1795017757000))\n              snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (map-constructors (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (every? #(strictly-ascending? (pair-keys %)) ctors)))))))\n  (testing \"the constant fast path stays a literal\"\n    (is (= {:type :literal :value {:a 1 :b 2}}\n           (yang/compile {:a 1 :b 2})))))\n\n\n(def ^:private set-corpus\n  \"The recorded corpus of dynamic set element lists.\"\n  [[:dynamic-elements\n    [(list '+ 'n 0) (list '+ 'n 1) (list 'first 'xs)]]\n   [:nested-dynamic-sets\n    [#{(list '+ 'n 1) 2} (list 'first 'xs) 3]]\n   [:colliding-value-expressions\n    ;; two different expressions that evaluate to the same value\n    [(list '- 'n 1) (list '- 1 'n) (list '+ 'n 0)]]\n   [:heterogeneous-elements\n    [:kw \"str\" 3 1.5 quoted-pair-key quoted-meta-key (list '+ 'n 2)]]])\n\n\n(deftest set-permutation-invariance-test\n  (testing \"sizes 0-4: every element permutation, both representations\"\n    (doseq [n (range 5)\n            :let [elements (sized-set-elements n)]]\n      (testing (str \"size \" n)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:vec-set :hash-set]]\n                                         (build-set rep (permute elements p)))))\n                             (all-permutations n))\n              snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (pos? (count variants)))\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (when (pos? n)\n            (doseq [form variants\n                    :let [ctors (collection-applications (yang/compile form))]]\n              (is (= 1 (count ctors)))\n              (is (every? #(strictly-ascending? (element-keys %)) ctors))))))))\n  (testing \"recorded corpus\"\n    (doseq [[label elements] set-corpus]\n      (testing (str label)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:vec-set :hash-set]]\n                                         (build-set rep (permute elements p)))))\n                             (all-permutations (count elements)))\n              snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (collection-applications (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (every? #(strictly-ascending? (element-keys %)) ctors)))))))\n  (testing \"sizes 8/9/16/32: recorded permutations\"\n    (doseq [n map-corpus-sizes\n            :let [elements (sized-set-elements n)]]\n      (testing (str \"size \" n)\n        (let [variants (into []\n                             (mapcat (fn [p]\n                                       (for [rep [:vec-set :hash-set]]\n                                         (build-set rep (permute elements p)))))\n                             (recorded-permutations n 1795017757001))\n              snaps (mapv compile-snapshot variants)]\n          (is (apply = snaps))\n          (doseq [form variants\n                  :let [ctors (collection-applications (yang/compile form))]]\n            (is (every? #(strictly-ascending? (element-keys %)) ctors)))))))\n  (testing \"compiled element occurrences survive: expressions that evaluate\n            to one value keep their compiled occurrences\"\n    (let [form #{(list '- 'n 1) (list '- 1 'n)}\n          ctor (first (collection-applications (yang/compile form)))]\n      (is (= 3 (count (:operands ctor))))\n      (is (= 2 (count (element-keys ctor))))))\n  (testing \"the constant fast path stays a literal\"\n    (is (= {:type :literal :value #{1 2 3}}\n           (yang/compile #{1 2 3})))))\n\n\n(defn- root-of\n  [ast]\n  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n\n\n      (is (= empty-map-seed-root (first roots)))\n      (is (odd? (count roots)))\n      (is (= (+ 1 (* 2 (count form))) (count roots)))\n      (is (strictly-ascending? pairs))\n      (is (= (independent-pair-keys form)\n             (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare pairs)))\n          \"the emitted pairs are exactly the independently compiled source\n           pairs, none lost or mixed\")))\n  (testing \"the value root breaks equal key roots\"\n    ;; two NaN keys are never = to each other (both survive the host map)\n    ;; and the codec makes every NaN one quiet NaN, so both compile to one\n    ;; key code: only the value root can order these pairs\n    (let [form (assoc {} ##NaN :left ##NaN (list '+ 'n 1))\n          ctor (last (map-constructors (yang/compile form)))\n          pairs (pair-keys ctor)]\n      (is (= 2 (count pairs)) (str \"both NaN entries survive: \" (count pairs)))\n      (is (strictly-ascending? pairs))\n      (is (= (first (first pairs)) (first (second pairs))))\n      (is (= (mapv second pairs)\n             (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare (mapv second pairs)))))))\n  (testing \"identical compiled pairs tie without occurrence loss\"\n    (let [form (assoc {} ##NaN (list '+ 'n 0) ##NaN (list '+ 'n 0))\n          ctor (last (map-constructors (yang/compile form)))\n          pairs (pair-keys ctor)]\n      (is (= 2 (count pairs)))\n      (is (= (first pairs) (second pairs)))\n      (is (= 5 (count (:operands ctor))) \"seed plus both pair occurrences\")))\n  (testing \"identical compiled set elements tie without occurrence loss\"\n    ;; two NaN elements are host-unequal (a NaN is never = to itself) and\n    ;; compile to one quiet-NaN row, so they are the whole-element tie.\n    ;; Retention is per constructor, not a map-vs-set difference: on the\n    ;; JVM, into over exactly the NaN pair keeps both (a persistent conj\n    ;; chain collapses them under Java equals, and one transient session\n    ;; that also mixes in a seq element loses one -- the r2 findings\n    ;; record the probe), so the pair is built and finalized before the\n    ;; dynamic element joins. That element is what keeps the set off the\n    ;; constant fast path so it reaches the emitter at all. On Node and\n    ;; Dart no constructor collapses the pair (= is === / Dart ==, and\n    ;; NaN never equals itself there).\n    (let [nan-key [(root-of (yang/compile-form ##NaN false {}))]\n          form (conj (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) (list '+ 'n 0))\n          ctor (first (collection-applications (yang/compile form)))\n          keys (element-keys ctor)]\n      (is (= 3 (count keys)) (str \"both NaN occurrences survive: \" (count keys)))\n      (is (= 2 (count (filter #(= nan-key %) keys)))\n          \"the tied element root appears exactly twice, not deduplicated\")\n      (is (= 1 (count (distinct (remove #(= nan-key %) keys))))\n          \"the third, distinct occurrence is retained beside the tie\")\n      (is (= (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare keys)) (vec keys))\n          \"the element vector equals its own non-descending sort: the tied\n           roots sit adjacent and nothing is reordered around them\")\n      (is (= 4 (count (:operands ctor))) \"seed plus all three occurrences\")))\n  (testing \"distinct dynamic set elements keep their compiled occurrences\"\n    (let [inner (list '+ 'n 0)\n          form #{inner (list '+ 'n 1)}\n          ctor (first (collection-applications (yang/compile form)))\n          keys (element-keys ctor)]\n      (is (= 2 (count keys)))\n      (is (strictly-ascending? keys))\n      (is (= 3 (count (:operands ctor))))))\n  (testing \"source-position and node metadata never choose the order\"\n    (let [plain {:a (list '+ 'n 1), :b (list '+ 'n 2)}\n          positioned (with-meta plain {:line 3 :column 4 :end-line 3 :end-column 9})\n          noted (with-meta plain {:note :source-form})\n          value-meta {(with-meta (list '+ 'n 1) {:line 8}) :a\n                      (list '+ 'n 2) :b}\n          snap (fn [f] (compile-snapshot f))\n          ctor-roots (fn [f] (child-roots (first (map-constructors (yang/compile f)))))]\n      (is (= (snap plain) (snap positioned)))\n      (is (= (snap plain) (snap noted)))\n      (is (= (ctor-roots plain) (ctor-roots positioned)))\n      (is (= (ctor-roots plain) (ctor-roots noted)))\n      (is (strictly-ascending? (pair-keys (first (map-constructors (yang/compile value-meta))))))))\n  (testing \"semantic metadata in literal payloads stays content\"\n    ;; the discriminating control (B4): two OTHERWISE IDENTICAL maps whose\n    ;; only difference is semantic (non-position) metadata inside one\n    ;; quoted literal key -- if the codec discarded that metadata the two\n    ;; programs would mint one root\n    (let [plain {(list (quote quote) [1 2]) (list (quote +) (quote n) 1),\n                 :other 0}\n          with-sem {(list (quote quote) (with-meta [1 2] {:sem true}))\n                    (list (quote +) (quote n) 1), :other 0}\n          with-empty-sem {(list (quote quote) (with-meta [1 2] {}))\n                          (list (quote +) (quote n) 1), :other 0}]\n      (is (not= (root-of (yang/compile plain))\n                (root-of (yang/compile with-sem)))\n          \"one semantic metadata key changes the literal payload content\")\n      (is (= (root-of (yang/compile plain))\n             (root-of (yang/compile with-empty-sem)))\n          \"empty metadata is no content: the payload matches the plain one\")\n      (is (strictly-ascending? (pair-keys (last (map-constructors\n                                                  (yang/compile with-sem)))))))))\n\n\n;; The outcome lane the arity payload check runs on: the same light\n;; convention clojure_test runs (default registry + stream/cell/data\n;; modules + the portable adapter), portable across the four hosts.\n(def ^:private outcome-modules\n  (let [host (fn [name entries]\n               (fn [registry]\n                 (module/register-host-module\n                   registry name\n                   (into {} (map (fn [[op f _]] [op f])) entries)\n                   (into {} (map (fn [[op _ p]] [op p])) entries))))\n        portable [['nth\n                   (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\n                                         (get data/data-module 'nth))\n                   (get data/data-profiles 'nth)]]]\n    (-> (module/default-registry)\n        module/register-stream-module\n        module/register-cell-module\n                      (every? #(constant-form? % false) (vals form)))\n     :else false)))\n\n\n(defn- content-root\n  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\n   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\n   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\n   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\n   root or ordering table.\"\n  [ast]\n  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-constructed-collection\n  \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n   existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n   elements like Clojure. Constant collections stay :literal nodes.\n\n   [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n   #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\n\n   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\n   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\n   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\n   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\n   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\n   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\n   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\n   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\n   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\n   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\n   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\n   vector retains its written element order.\"\n  [form tail? env macro-env]\n  (let [ctor (cond\n               (vector? form) ['conj []]\n               (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n               :else ['assoc {}])\n        [op seed] ctor\n        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\n        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\n        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\n        sorted-children\n        (cond\n          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\n          (map? form)\n          {:order :canonical\n           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\n                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\n                                  cv (compile-child v)]\n                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\n                               :children [ck cv]}))\n                          (keys form) (vals form))}\n          :else\n          {:order :canonical\n           :records (mapv (fn [e]\n                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\n                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\n                               :children [ce]}))\n                          form)})\n        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\n                   :written (:children sorted-children)\n                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\n                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\n                                  (:records sorted-children))))\n        call {:type :application,\n              :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\n              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}] operands)}]\n    (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(def initial-macro-env\n  \"Compile-time map of macro names known before any defmacro: none. The\n   standard forms live in the expander's store, not here.\"\n  {})\n\n\n(defn- shadow-macro-env\n  \"Remove shadowed names from the macro environment.\"\n  [macro-env names]\n  (apply dissoc macro-env names))\n\n\n(defn clojure-manifest\n  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it.\n   Revision c1-2 additionally declares the constructed-collections\n   lowering profile: a dynamically constructed map or set literal now\n   orders its constructor operands by compiled content\n   (:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1), a one-time canonical\n   shift for affected newly compiled artifacts; the C1 support claim,\n   the C1 marker value and the execution grammar versions are\n   unchanged.\"\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-2\"\n         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
